IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sfa-market-conduct`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001, Part 12 Divisions 1, 3 and 4 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_sfa.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

`a trader who painted the tape to lure buyers` MEANS TradingConduct WITH
    `a purpose was to create a false appearance` IS TRUE
    `created or was likely to create a false appearance` IS FALSE
    `knew or was reckless as to that effect` IS FALSE
    `was a wash trade or matched orders` IS FALSE
    `the defendant proved no such purpose` IS FALSE

`a wash trade between two accounts of the same owner` MEANS TradingConduct WITH
    `a purpose was to create a false appearance` IS FALSE
    `created or was likely to create a false appearance` IS FALSE
    `knew or was reckless as to that effect` IS FALSE
    `was a wash trade or matched orders` IS TRUE
    `the defendant proved no such purpose` IS FALSE

`a wash trade the owner proved was for tax reasons` MEANS TradingConduct WITH
    `a purpose was to create a false appearance` IS FALSE
    `created or was likely to create a false appearance` IS FALSE
    `knew or was reckless as to that effect` IS FALSE
    `was a wash trade or matched orders` IS TRUE
    `the defendant proved no such purpose` IS TRUE

`a large order reckless as to its effect on the price` MEANS TradingConduct WITH
    `a purpose was to create a false appearance` IS FALSE
    `created or was likely to create a false appearance` IS TRUE
    `knew or was reckless as to that effect` IS TRUE
    `was a wash trade or matched orders` IS FALSE
    `the defendant proved no such purpose` IS FALSE

`a large order that moved the price unforeseeably` MEANS TradingConduct WITH
    `a purpose was to create a false appearance` IS FALSE
    `created or was likely to create a false appearance` IS TRUE
    `knew or was reckless as to that effect` IS FALSE
    `was a wash trade or matched orders` IS FALSE
    `the defendant proved no such purpose` IS FALSE

`a deliberately false profit announcement` MEANS Statement WITH
    `false or misleading in a material particular` IS TRUE
    `likely to induce dealing or move the price` IS TRUE
    `the maker knew` IS TRUE
    `the maker ought reasonably to have known` IS FALSE
    `the maker did not care whether it was true` IS FALSE

`a careless announcement the director ought to have checked` MEANS Statement WITH
    `false or misleading in a material particular` IS TRUE
    `likely to induce dealing or move the price` IS TRUE
    `the maker knew` IS FALSE
    `the maker ought reasonably to have known` IS TRUE
    `the maker did not care whether it was true` IS FALSE

`a reckless forum post about a penny stock` MEANS Statement WITH
    `false or misleading in a material particular` IS TRUE
    `likely to induce dealing or move the price` IS TRUE
    `the maker knew` IS FALSE
    `the maker ought reasonably to have known` IS FALSE
    `the maker did not care whether it was true` IS TRUE

`an honest error that no one could reasonably have caught` MEANS Statement WITH
    `false or misleading in a material particular` IS TRUE
    `likely to induce dealing or move the price` IS TRUE
    `the maker knew` IS FALSE
    `the maker ought reasonably to have known` IS FALSE
    `the maker did not care whether it was true` IS FALSE

`a false but immaterial statement` MEANS Statement WITH
    `false or misleading in a material particular` IS FALSE
    `likely to induce dealing or move the price` IS TRUE
    `the maker knew` IS TRUE
    `the maker ought reasonably to have known` IS FALSE
    `the maker did not care whether it was true` IS FALSE

`a director who bought before an unannounced takeover` MEANS InsiderCase WITH
    `the person is connected to the company` IS TRUE
    `possessed the information` IS TRUE
    `the information was generally available` IS FALSE
    `the information was price-sensitive` IS TRUE
    `actually knew it was inside information` IS TRUE
    `ought reasonably to have known it was inside information` IS FALSE
    `rebutted the presumption of knowledge` IS FALSE
    `the information was only of their own intended dealing` IS FALSE
    `the counterparty knew or ought to have known it` IS FALSE
    `dealt or procured dealing` IS TRUE

